    <bpmn:process id="W_W4736" name="W4736. Third-Party Incident, Breach &amp; Performance-Degradation Handling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Third-party incident (cyber breach, financial failure, operational outage, compliance breach, performance degradation)
Frequency: Per incident
Volume: ~25–50 incidents/year across the third-party base (mostly minor lapses)
Owner: TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Participants: Cyber IR (VS-27.3 W383), Privacy (VS-91), BCP (VS-26), Fraud (VS-125), Legal (VS-100.3), business owners, the third party
Source: workflow W4736 — Third-Party Incident, Breach &amp; Performance-Degradation Handling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4736_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4736_Lane1" name="TPRM Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4736_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4736_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4736_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4736_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4736_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4736_Start3" name="Third-party incident (cyber breach, financial failure, operational outage, compliance…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4736_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4736_Task4" name="Intake and triage third-party incidents: cyber breach (coordinate VS-27.3…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Intake and triage third-party incidents: cyber breach (coordinate VS-27.3 W383), privacy breach (VS-91 72-hour notification), operational outage (VS-26 BCP activation), financial failure (supply disruption VS-02.3), compliance breach (VS-22), performance degradation (VS-67)
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Domain Owners
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4736_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4736_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4736_Task5" name="Manage incident response: activate BuildRight&#x27;s response per the affected…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manage incident response: activate BuildRight&#x27;s response per the affected domain, demand the third party&#x27;s incident response, assess BuildRight impact (data/operations/customers), and coordinate notification (regulators, customers, board W4728) as required
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Domain Owners / Legal
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / VP Legal
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4736_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4736_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4736_Task6" name="Conduct post-incident review; capture lessons; adjust tiering (W4723), DD…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Conduct post-incident review; capture lessons; adjust tiering (W4723), DD (W4729), monitoring (W4734), and contracts; manage third-party accountability (remediation, credit, termination W4740)
Responsible (R): TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / Legal
Accountable (A): TPRM Lead / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Post-incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4736_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4736_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4736_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4736_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-714 (ensure controlled execution — Due Diligence, Continuous Monitoring &amp; Evidence Lifecycle (PA-161.2).) | - CTL-714: third-party incidents triaged and managed per domain; notification deadlines met (VS-91); post-incident lessons captured
Owner: TPRM Program Manager / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
